    "interpretation": "When uvm_tracker_add_tracker_safe() sees NV_ERR_NO_MEMORY after the merge's reserve/prune/retry sequence, it waits for the source tracker. uvm_pmm_gpu_free() calls that helper while holding the root-chunk bitlock; source callsites include GPU-chunk cleanup under the VA-block mutex. This is a conditional latency and progress risk under allocation pressure, not a demonstrated deadlock or an observed runtime failure. The bitlock is sleepable (wait_on_bit_lock), so this audit does not classify it as a spinlock/atomic-context violation. The isolated provider guard in pmm_gpu_alloc() does not guard pmm_gpu_free(); the free path does not revalidate tracker GPU/provider identity, and same-GPU fallback waits remain possible.",
